# Utilities & Helpers Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines define patterns for implementing utility functions, helper classes, and extensions in the Flutter Chat App. They apply to all shared functionality that doesn't fit into the service or repository categories. Following these guidelines ensures code reusability, maintainability, and consistency throughout the codebase.

## Best Practices

### Utility Functions
- Create pure, stateless utility functions for common operations
- Group related functions in thematic utility classes
- Prefer static methods for utility functions
- Provide detailed documentation for complex utilities
- Write comprehensive unit tests for all utilities
- Handle edge cases and null values gracefully
- Implement error handling for utilities that might fail
- Keep utility functions focused on a single responsibility
- Use generics to make utilities more flexible
- Avoid side effects in utility functions

### Extensions
- Use extensions to add functionality to existing classes
- Keep extensions focused on a specific theme or functionality
- Document extensions clearly, especially for third-party classes
- Implement extensions that feel natural to the extended class
- Use extensions to improve code readability and reduce boilerplate
- Name extension methods to clearly indicate their purpose
- Avoid name conflicts with existing methods in extended classes
- Group related extensions in a single file
- Prefer extension methods over utility functions for class-specific operations
- Test extensions thoroughly with different parameter values

### Constants and Enums
- Create dedicated files for related constants
- Use meaningful names for constants and enums
- Group related constants in classes or objects
- Prefer enums over string constants for fixed sets of values
- Add helper methods to enums for common operations
- Document the purpose and valid values for constants
- Make constants immutable (final/const) where appropriate
- Use named constants instead of magic numbers or strings
- Consider internationalization needs when creating string constants
- Create extension methods for enums to add behavior

## File / Project Structure Guidelines

```
lib/
  ├── utils/              # Utility functions and helpers
  │   ├── formatters/     # String, date, and number formatting utilities
  │   ├── validators/     # Validation utilities
