## Coding & Styling Conventions

### Utility Functions
- Name utility classes with a clear purpose suffix (e.g., `StringUtils`, `DateUtils`)
- Name utility methods with verb phrases that describe their action
- Use proper parameter types rather than `dynamic`
- Implement proper null safety for all parameters
- Add appropriate default values for optional parameters
- Use named parameters for methods with multiple optional arguments
- Return sensible defaults for error cases
- Add example usage in documentation comments
- Keep methods focused and under 20 lines when possible

### Extensions
- Name extension files after the extended class (e.g., `string_extensions.dart`)
- Name the extension using the pattern `${ClassName}Ext` (e.g., `StringExt`)
- Group multiple extensions on the same class in a single file
- Document expected behavior for edge cases
- Keep extension methods short and focused
- Make extension methods feel like natural additions to the class

### Constants
- Use `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` for true constants
- Use `kConstantName` for Flutter/Dart style constants
- Use `PascalCase` for enum types and values
- Group related constants in classes with a private constructor
- Prefer typed constants over strings when possible

## Implementation Examples

### Utility Class Example
```dart
/// Utilities for string manipulation and formatting
class StringUtils {
  // Private constructor to prevent instantiation
  StringUtils._();
  
  /// Truncates a string to a maximum length and adds an ellipsis if needed
  ///
  /// Example: `StringUtils.truncate("Hello World", 7)` returns "Hello..."
  static String truncate(String text, int maxLength, {String ellipsis = '...'}) {
    if (text.length <= maxLength) {
      return text;
    }
    
    return '${text.substring(0, maxLength - ellipsis.length)}$ellipsis';
  }
  
  /// Capitalizes the first letter of a string
  ///
  /// Example: `StringUtils.capitalize("hello")` returns "Hello"
  static String capitalize(String text) {
    if (text.isEmpty) return text;
    return '${text[0].toUpperCase()}${text.substring(1)}';
  }
  
  /// Converts a string to title case (capitalizes first letter of each word)
  ///
  /// Example: `StringUtils.toTitleCase("hello world")` returns "Hello World"
  static String toTitleCase(String text) {
    if (text.isEmpty) return text;
    
    return text.split(' ')
        .map((word) => capitalize(word))
        .join(' ');
  }
  
  /// Removes all HTML tags from a string
  ///
  /// Example: `StringUtils.stripHtml("<p>Hello</p>")` returns "Hello"
  static String stripHtml(String htmlString) {
    final regex = RegExp(r'<[^>]*>');
    return htmlString.replaceAll(regex, '');
  }
}
```

### Extension Example
```dart
/// Extensions on DateTime for common date operations and formatting
extension DateTimeExt on DateTime {
  /// Check if date is today
  bool get isToday {
    final now = DateTime.now();
    return year == now.year && month == now.month && day == now.day;
  }
  
  /// Check if date is yesterday
  bool get isYesterday {
    final yesterday = DateTime.now().subtract(const Duration(days: 1));
    return year == yesterday.year && month == yesterday.month && day == yesterday.day;
  }
  
  /// Check if date is tomorrow
  bool get isTomorrow {
    final tomorrow = DateTime.now().add(const Duration(days: 1));
    return year == tomorrow.year && month == tomorrow.month && day == tomorrow.day;
  }
  
  /// Format as relative date (Today, Yesterday, or date)
  String toRelativeDate() {
    if (isToday) {
      return 'Today';
    } else if (isYesterday) {
      return 'Yesterday';
    } else {
      final formatter = DateFormat('MMM d, yyyy');
      return formatter.format(this);
    }
  }
  
  /// Format time as 12-hour format with AM/PM
  String to12HourTime() {
    final formatter = DateFormat('h:mm a');
    return formatter.format(this);
  }
  
  /// Format time as 24-hour format
  String to24HourTime() {
    final formatter = DateFormat('HH:mm');
    return formatter.format(this);
  }
  
  /// Get start of day (midnight)
  DateTime get startOfDay => DateTime(year, month, day);
  
  /// Get end of day (23:59:59.999)
  DateTime get endOfDay => DateTime(year, month, day, 23, 59, 59, 999);
  
  /// Add days to date
  DateTime addDays(int days) => add(Duration(days: days));
  
  /// Subtract days from date
  DateTime subtractDays(int days) => subtract(Duration(days: days));
}
```

