### Enum with Extension Example
```dart
/// Message status in the system
enum MessageStatus {
  sending,
  sent,
  delivered,
  read,
  failed,
  deleted;
}

/// Extension to add functionality to MessageStatus enum
extension MessageStatusExt on MessageStatus {
  /// Whether the message is considered delivered to the recipient
  bool get isDelivered => this == MessageStatus.delivered || this == MessageStatus.read;
  
  /// Whether the message has been successfully sent to the server
  bool get isSent => this == MessageStatus.sent || isDelivered;
  
  /// Whether the message has failed to send
  bool get hasFailed => this == MessageStatus.failed;
  
  /// Whether the message is in a terminal state
  bool get isTerminalState => this == MessageStatus.read || 
                              this == MessageStatus.failed || 
                              this == MessageStatus.deleted;
  
  /// Get localized display string for this status
  String getDisplayName(BuildContext context) {
    switch (this) {
      case MessageStatus.sending:
        return context.l10n.messageSending;
      case MessageStatus.sent:
        return context.l10n.messageSent;
      case MessageStatus.delivered:
        return context.l10n.messageDelivered;
      case MessageStatus.read:
        return context.l10n.messageRead;
      case MessageStatus.failed:
        return context.l10n.messageFailed;
      case MessageStatus.deleted:
        return context.l10n.messageDeleted;
    }
  }
  
  /// Get icon for this status
  IconData getIcon() {
    switch (this) {
      case MessageStatus.sending:
        return Icons.access_time;
      case MessageStatus.sent:
        return Icons.check;
      case MessageStatus.delivered:
        return Icons.done_all;
      case MessageStatus.read:
        return Icons.done_all;
      case MessageStatus.failed:
        return Icons.error_outline;
      case MessageStatus.deleted:
        return Icons.delete_outline;
    }
  }
  
  /// Get color for this status
  Color getColor(BuildContext context) {
    final colorScheme = Theme.of(context).colorScheme;
    
    switch (this) {
      case MessageStatus.sending:
        return colorScheme.onSurface.withOpacity(0.5);
      case MessageStatus.sent:
        return colorScheme.onSurface.withOpacity(0.7);
      case MessageStatus.delivered:
        return colorScheme.primary;
      case MessageStatus.read:
        return colorScheme.primary;
      case MessageStatus.failed:
        return colorScheme.error;
      case MessageStatus.deleted:
        return colorScheme.onSurface.withOpacity(0.5);
    }
  }
}
```

## Performance & Optimization Tips
- Cache results of expensive utility operations
- Use const constructors for static utility classes
- Implement lazy initialization for resource-intensive helpers
- Avoid creating unnecessary objects in frequently called utilities
- Use memoization for pure functions with expensive calculations
- Keep utility functions lightweight and focused
- Use extension methods for better code organization and readability
- Consider using isolates for CPU-intensive utility operations
- Optimize string operations in heavily used utilities
- Use efficient algorithms and data structures

## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Write comprehensive unit tests for all utility functions
- Test edge cases and boundary conditions
- Verify handling of null and empty inputs
- Test performance for utilities used in tight loops
- Write tests for each extension method
- Verify constants have expected values
- Use parameterized tests for functions with different input variations
- Test enum helper methods and extensions
- Benchmark performance-critical utilities
- Verify internationalization works with utilities that handle text
- Test format utilities with various locale settings
